'''Nintendo Music''' is a [[music streaming service]] by [[Nintendo]] that features their [[video game soundtracks]]. The service is available for [[Nintendo Switch Online]] users, a [[subscription service]] otherwise for the [[Nintendo Switch]] and [[Nintendo Switch 2]] video game consoles. Nintendo Music launched for [[Android (operating system)|Android]] and [[iOS]] on October 31, 2024, with a web player added on June 1, 2026. In addition to music streaming, features for extended music playback and [[Spoiler (media)|spoiler prevention]] are available to users. Themed playlists appear based on Nintendo franchises, characters, and general moods, with video game screenshots representing each track. It is the first widely accessible digital platform for Nintendo's soundtracks, with previous video games receiving soundtrack [[CD|CDs]] exclusively in Japan or through [[limited edition]] game releases.

Nintendo Music has received mixed reviews. Praise was given for its curated playlists, extendable tracks, and the ever-expanding library of soundtracks since launch. Fans and journalists have criticized the app for its exclusion of composer credits, the lack of available songs during its initial launch, and limited music offerings in "special release" playlists. As of November 2024, the app has been downloaded by over one million users.

{{Short description|2019 book by Mai Thi Nguyen-Kim}}
{{italic title}}
'''''Chemistry for Breakfast: The Amazing Science of Everyday Life''''' ({{langx|de|'''Komisch, alles chemisch! Handys, Kaffee, Emotionen – wie man mit Chemie wirklich alles erklären kann'''}}<!--Same book as per https://catalog.mountainview.gov/Record/.b27872099 , Original German title from https://portal.dnb.de/opac.htm?method=simpleSearch&cqlMode=true&query=idn%3D1237277027-->) is a non-fiction book by [[Mai Thi Nguyen-Kim]], published in 2019 by [[Droemer Verlag]]. Claire Lenkova did the illustration work.

The English version, translated by Sarah Pybus,<!--https://portal.dnb.de/opac.htm?method=simpleSearch&cqlMode=true&query=idn%3D1237277027--> was published by [[Greystone Books]] in 2021.<ref name=Smith>{{cite web|last=Smith|first=Wade-Lee|url=https://www.libraryjournal.com:443/review/chemistry-for-breakfast-the-amazing-science-of-everyday-life-2110842|title=Chemistry for Breakfast: The Amazing Science of Everyday Life |magazine=[[Library Journal]]|date=2021-02-26}}</ref>

Nguyen-Kim stated that she wanted to show that chemistry can be interesting.<ref name=Schneider>{{cite web|last=Schneider|first=Wolfgang|url=https://www.faz.net/aktuell/feuilleton/buecher/rezensionen/sachbuch/hoerbuch-der-chemie-youtuberin-mai-thi-nguyen-kim-mailab-16140993.html|title=Sie hat noch eine Reaktion am Laufen|newspaper=[[Frankfurter Allgemeine]]|language=de|date=2019-04-29|access-date=2024-11-05|quote=Die Wissenschaft ist zu interessant, um sie den Fachleuten zu überlassen – so ihre Devise[...]}}</ref> Wade-Lee Smith of the [[University of Toledo]] library described the style as using "analogies and simple illustrations" to make chemistry comprehensible to the lay public, and that the tone is "casual and familiar".<ref name=Smith/>

An editor of ''[[Science (journal)|Science Magazine]]'', Marc S. Lavine, wrote that the book's goal is establishing critical thinking instead of encouraging readers to pursue a career in science.<ref name=Lavine>{{cite journal|last=Lavine|first=Marc S.|url=https://www.sciencemagazinedigital.org/sciencemagazine/03_december_2021/MobilePagedArticle.action?articleId=1747938#articleId1747938|title=Chemistry for Breakfast: The Amazing Science of Everyday Life|journal=[[Science (journal)|Science]]|date=2021-12-03|access-date=2024-11-05}}</ref>

